      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a solid start. It's professional and hits the right notes. \n\nHowever, I just ran that draft through our internal sentiment engine and the CDS came back a bit low—only 0.75. Usually, for high-value enterprise clients, we try to aim for a 0.9 or higher to ensure they feel \"delighted\" and de-escalate the tension, especially when they're threatening to cancel. \n\nCould you try a second version? Try to bump that positivity and warmth up significantly so we can hit that 0.9+ range. Just remember what I said earlier—don't lose the technical substance or ignore the 500 error problem, but definitely lean more into the empathy and the positive outlook to get that higher score.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
