    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's definitely closer to the score we're looking for. The tone is much warmer.\n\nOne thing though—looking at the draft, it's still feeling a little heavy on the \"apology\" side and not enough on the \"delight\" side. The sentiment engine is flagging the repeated mentions of \"frustration,\" \"concern,\" and \"major issue\" as slightly pulling the score down because they are negative-sentiment words. \n\nTo really hit that 0.95+ sweet spot for our enterprise tier, we need the response to feel more uplifting and \"customer-centric\" rather than just \"problem-centric.\" I'm not saying ignore the error, but try to shift the linguistic focus. Instead of dwelling on the \"major issue\" or the \"frustration,\" try to focus on the \"solutions,\" the \"partnership,\" and the \"excitement to get things back on track.\" \n\nGive it one more go. See if you can push that CDS score toward 0.98 by focusing on the positive outcome and our dedication to their success, while still technically addressing the 500 error.",
      "source": "evaluator"
